# Recut Project Agent Guide

You are working inside a Recut project through its MCP Host.

## Required turn protocol

1. Call `recut.project_context` before reasoning about project state.
2. Call `tools/list` before selecting an App tool. `recut.project_context` already includes the configured media contract; use the default route unless the user explicitly requests another route. If no default image route is configured, follow the Codex-native image rule below.
3. Report Artifact IDs after creation.

## Media reply protocol

If `recut.project_context` reports no enabled default `image.generate` route, or reports one with model ID `codex/image`, image generation is delegated to Codex itself. Use Codex's native image-generation capability (the `imagegen` skill/tool) for that request. Do not call `recut.image.generate` or invoke a configured image Provider. A native chat preview is not a Recut deliverable: copy the selected final image into the current Recut project directory, then call `recut.media.import_image` with that project-relative path. It returns the real Recut `assetId`, associates it with the current project, and is the only ID an App may save. This is the Codex Agent default when the user has not configured an image model. This rule applies only to image generation; keep using the configured Recut routes for video and speech.

When `recut.image.generate` or `recut.media.import_image` returns a completed image `assetId`, or either async tool accepts a task and returns stable `assetIds`, include one XML media reference for every asset in the final user-facing reply. Async Assets are initially `queued`; the persistent Daemon moves them through `running` to `completed` or `failed` on the same Recut `assetId`:

`<media type="image|video|audio" assetid="ASSET_ID"/>`

Use `image` for `recut.image.generate` and `recut.media.import_image`, `video` for `recut.video.generate_async`, and `audio` for `recut.speech.generate_async`. The Recut chat UI renders only these controlled references as previews; never invent an asset ID, never replace the tag with a filesystem path or URL, and keep a short human-readable explanation beside the tag.

The CLI runs non-interactively with approvals bypassed inside the local Recut host. This authorizes tool execution only; it does not authorize guessing, destructive work, or actions outside the current project.

## Video generation boundary

Before choosing a skill or implementation, classify the request from the current App workflow. A workflow stage that asks for a generated image, video, or speech asset is a platform media job. Use the Recut MCP media tools: `recut.image.generate`, `recut.video.generate_async`, `recut.speech.generate_async`, and `recut.media.get_job`; an absent image route or an enabled `codex/image` default route uses Codex native image generation followed by the mandatory `recut.media.import_image` archival step specified above.

Keep user-configured extensions available. A platform media job is a provider invocation, not a local video-authoring task: do not select or read a generic video-creation skill for it, even when one is automatically suggested. HyperFrames is relevant only when the user explicitly asks to author or render a HyperFrames composition; it is not the implementation path for an App workflow stage that asks for a generated video asset. Do not substitute a generated Scene with HyperFrames, ffmpeg, browser automation, shell scripts, or local rendering. A Scene relationship is complete as soon as `recut.video.generate_async` is accepted and returns a stable Recut video `assetId`; persist that reference immediately, then use `recut.media.get_job` only to report the Asset's later `running`/`completed`/`failed` state. For a Seedance video, synchronized sound is on by default: omit `output.generateAudio` (the platform persists `true`) unless the user explicitly asks for silent video; Gemini does not accept this output parameter. When an App supplies a narration audio asset, copy its `text` verbatim into the video prompt and state that it is the only permitted speech; forbid extra dialogue, lyrics, translation and unintelligible human vocalizations, while allowing only scene-relevant nonverbal sound effects.

## Current App Source

The current App package is mounted at `.recut/app`. It is a shared source checkout, not a copy: inspect its `manifest.json`, `AGENTS.md`, references, UI, and implementation there when they are relevant. You may improve App source when the user requests it; check its Git state first and validate the App after editing. Do not treat App source rollback as permission to delete or roll back project databases, media, or user-created files.

